# Vivado output.  Every path below is regenerated by `make` from the ground source that
# lives beside it -- hdmi_xcku5p.xpr, hdmi_xcku5p.srcs/, build.tcl and the .tcl hooks -- so
# none of it belongs in git.
#
# Tracking it once cost a build.  Only *part* of these trees had been committed, so a
# `git clean -fdx` deleted the untracked half (ddr4_0's out-of-context checkpoint) while
# git restored the tracked half, and synthesis then died two seconds into elaboration
# with "module 'ddr4_0' not found" -- a state no Make target could repair.  build.tcl's
# ensure_ip_products now rebuilds any IP whose checkpoint is missing; that only stays
# true if a partial snapshot of these trees is never committed again.
hdmi_xcku5p.cache/
hdmi_xcku5p.gen/
hdmi_xcku5p.hw/
hdmi_xcku5p.runs/
hdmi_xcku5p.sim/
ddr4_0_ex.gen/
ddr4_0_ex.srcs/
.Xil/
vivado*.jou
vivado*.log

# ILA debug cores are created on demand by build.tcl (ILA_IRQ=1, ILA_PARITY=1, ...)
# straight into this directory; ddr4_0.xci is the only hand-configured IP here.  A stale
# ila_irq/ left on disk is why Vivado once had to name a second copy ila_irq_1.
hdmi_xcku5p.srcs/sources_1/ip/ila_*/

# Run-generated fileset: build.tcl adds its hook scripts here, and a 2 MB synthesis
# checkpoint was imported into it once and then tracked.
hdmi_xcku5p.srcs/utils_1/
